-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
PLACEHOLDER: The repository owner must generate a real RSA-4096 key pair
offline and replace this file with the actual public key PEM.

Generation instructions (run offline, never on the agent host):
  openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:4096 \
    -out custodian_private.pem
  openssl pkey -pubout -in custodian_private.pem \
    -out custodian_public_key.pem

Requirements:
- Key type: RSA only (EC keys are incompatible with the RSA-OAEP implementation)
- Key size: exactly 4096 bits
- Public exponent: 65537
- Preflight will reject any key that does not meet these requirements

Custody rules:
- custodian_private.pem must NEVER be committed to version control
- custodian_private.pem must be stored in a location inaccessible to any
  agent or evaluator process (password manager, encrypted offline storage,
  or sealed physical envelope)
- Only this file (custodian_public_key.pem) is committed to the repository

Offline deblinding (after all evaluator outputs are collected and frozen):
  python poc6c/blinding.py deblind \
    --bundle blinding-outputs/mapping_bundle.json \
    --private-key /path/to/custodian_private.pem

Cryptographic design note:
- The blinding seed (CONFIRMATION_BLIND_SEED) is used only for HMAC-SHA256
  arm assignment; it is never used as or derived into an encryption key
- A fresh random DEK is generated for each blinding operation
- The DEK is encrypted with AES-256-GCM and the resulting ciphertext is
  wrapped under this RSA-4096 public key using RSA-OAEP (SHA-256/MGF1-SHA-256)
-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
